From 953d1fc8d8c9f487135287ec75500dc56e20bf8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redgrave961 <214504937+Redgrave961@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:11:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run firmware SPURS (libsre) for real: SPU side, residency,
 PRX call ABI

- tools/lift_firmware_spu.py lifts a relocated firmware module's embedded SPU
  ELFs and the code bodies it streams into local store, with every absolute
  stack set (il/ila/lqa $r1) as a stack-reset entry and call return entries.
  Adapted from the inFAMOUS 2 port's toolkit (SamiEnazi/ps3recomp 70c456e).
- spu_overlay_register_region_at: a code region lifted for one LS address is
  resident whenever its own bytes land there, whatever the GET's source (the
  taskset module loads tasks in pieces and restores them from context saves).
  A GET of zeros or of the region's own bytes no longer evicts it.
- Fast indirect dispatch and the drain resume use spu_lifted_lookup, so
  resident code spans dispatch without the slow path.
- The taskset syscall intercept is HLE only when no policy code is present at
  0xA70 (resident spans included); real tasks enter Sony's module.
- stop 0x101/0x102 unwind to the thread's landing pad; driver unwinds drop
  stale interrupt frames.
- Blocking channel reads and interpreting unlifted LS code are the default.
- build_spu_workloads --return-entries / --guest-regions (CMake
  PS3RECOMP_SPU_RETURN_ENTRIES / PS3RECOMP_SPU_GUEST_REGIONS) for titles whose
  tasks run under the firmware policy modules.
- PRX exports run on the caller's r1: the 0x1000 stack drop corrupted every
  argument passed in the parameter save area (Asura's 14-argument
  _cellSpursJobChainAttributeInitialize returned INVAL).
